cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this tutorial, please cite it using these metadata.
type: software
title: SGTL earthquake source tutorial
abstract: A hands-on Jupyter tutorial that takes a newcomer from earthquake catalogs and seismograms to
  research-level earthquake source characterization (picking, location, double-difference relocation,
  focal mechanisms, moment tensors, Coulomb stress, detection), built around the PocketQuake toolchain.
  Learners write the core methods themselves and check them against independent references.
authors:
- given-names: Minseong
  family-names: Seo
  affiliation: SGTL (Seismology, Geophysics, Tectonophysics Laboratory), Seoul National University
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-15
license:
